[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4493276759","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119568#issuecomment-4493276759","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119568","id":4493276759,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABC9H2Vw","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-20T00:10:02Z","updated_at":"2026-05-20T00:10:38Z","body":"I'm having a hard time seeing what's wrong on the videos, not only due to the low bitrate, but also because there's no comparison with SSR disabled (or the old SSR).\n\nI made a comparison with the MRP in Movie Maker mode at 60 FPS:\n\n### 4.5.1.stable\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/3549a1d8-3f5e-4349-bd36-a72f80a30b3e\n\n### 4.7.beta2\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8ff8ebcd-5125-47c4-b8b3-0f9989c4c9da\n\nSSR performs reprojection over one frame, which is why it has a delay of 1 frame and isn't visible in the first rendered frame in the 4.7 video. See discussion starting from https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111210#issuecomment-3418554715 in the SSR overhaul PR.\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4493276759/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4494417274","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119568#issuecomment-4494417274","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119568","id":4494417274,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABC-Ndeg","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-20T04:08:36Z","updated_at":"2026-05-20T04:08:36Z","body":"@Calinou I think the difference is that the glowing red box is not visible in the reflection when moving towards the camera. Which indicates our reprojection code is slightly wrong for translations. Its probably also broken for SSIL since they work the same AFAIK","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4494417274/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4496635859","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119568#issuecomment-4496635859","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119568","id":4496635859,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABDAU30w","user":{"login":"mrjustaguy","id":50302479,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwMzAyNDc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/50302479?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy","html_url":"https://github.com/mrjustaguy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-20T09:18:20Z","updated_at":"2026-05-20T09:18:20Z","body":"SSR while Static (game paused):\n\n<img width=\"247\" height=\"324\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5af1413b-8a78-46fa-94d7-41590ff18767\" />\n\nSSR while Dynamic (moving forward):\n\n<img width=\"277\" height=\"328\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/34375659-3b93-4da1-ab25-6db10b863f24\" />\n\nAs can be seen the Orange emission is suddenly appearing in a different place due to movement happening in the 2nd image, lagging behind.\n\nIn the 2nd video it's particularly obvious if I'm accelerating or not based on the lower two wings getting a blue trail when in motion.\n\nAnd yes the red box is not glowing in the reflection, but what's worse and not shown well in the MRP is that actually that Red box is now adding Red reflections to the wrong positions instead of just being absent\n\nAlso for clarification on the videos, all the lighting beyond the Glow is SSR, and any changes in lighting occuring beyond the Directional Light is due to SSR failing, and with the Old SSR there would be no lighting changes present beyond the DL.\n\nSadly I cannot make a Before anymore because the game has since stopped working on 4.5, though I do know this was not an issue of the old SSR as I have tested it back when the PR was fresh, which is Why I commented on it stating that it caused a major regression\n\nAs far as SSIL goes it should break too, however It's significantly subtler effect which is likely why it was never noticed.\n\nAlso to be clear, I'm not using SSR in my game, nor did I ever intend to before or after the overhaul, it just made for an interesting test setup that immediately threw these issues into my face so to speak.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4496635859/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4497590061","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119568#issuecomment-4497590061","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119568","id":4497590061,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABDBPHLQ","user":{"login":"blueskythlikesclouds","id":19259897,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MjU5ODk3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19259897?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds","html_url":"https://github.com/blueskythlikesclouds","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-20T10:50:31Z","updated_at":"2026-05-20T10:54:44Z","body":"> I think the difference is that the glowing red box is not visible in the reflection when moving towards the camera. Which indicates our reprojection code is slightly wrong for translations. Its probably also broken for SSIL since they work the same AFAIK\n\nIt's not wrong, it's just not accounting for everything. The reprojection is only done for the camera, so for static objects, it'll look correct, but for moving objects, we need proper motion vector information. So this is not a bug, rather a lacking implementation.\n\nI'm 100% sure it'll look correct with SSR using motion vectors. The tracing is done on the depth buffer of the current frame, but the color information is gathered from the previous. We just need to know where _actually_ the moving object was in the previous frame, instead of approximating it through the reprojection matrix.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4497590061/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4500047726","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119568#issuecomment-4500047726","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119568","id":4500047726,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABDDlHbg","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-20T15:40:08Z","updated_at":"2026-05-20T15:40:08Z","body":"@blueskythlikesclouds I'm not so sure it's about motion vectors. In screen space the objects aren't moving. So the motion vectors should be 0 anyway. ","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4500047726/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4500377789","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119568#issuecomment-4500377789","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119568","id":4500377789,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABDD5QvQ","user":{"login":"blueskythlikesclouds","id":19259897,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MjU5ODk3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19259897?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds","html_url":"https://github.com/blueskythlikesclouds","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-20T16:15:52Z","updated_at":"2026-05-20T16:17:23Z","body":"Sure, but the camera is moving. In SSR overhaul, I made reprojection take camera movement into account. So when an object moves, that makes it act like the object's world transform in the previous frame was the same as the current one, which is wrong. This works for static objects but not dynamic ones.\n\nEven if there's no camera movement, a dynamic object will still look wrong because we assume it keeps staying at the same world transform. Motion vectors would be the solution to this.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4500377789/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4500409405","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119568#issuecomment-4500409405","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119568","id":4500409405,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABDD7MPQ","user":{"login":"mrjustaguy","id":50302479,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwMzAyNDc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/50302479?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy","html_url":"https://github.com/mrjustaguy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-20T16:19:57Z","updated_at":"2026-05-20T16:19:57Z","body":"yeah dynamic objects reflected in static world would look just as bad, and only static worlds work fully with the SSR overhaul, anything dynamic will break somewhere somehow (beyond the camera itself)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4500409405/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]